@host = http://localhost:5048
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080
@realm = finance

### Get a token (captures access_token for the requests below)
# @name login
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=finance-web&username=testuser&password=password

### Store the token
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### No token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/expenses

### With token → 200 (empty or your expenses)
GET {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an expense (belongs to testuser) → 201
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "amount": 42.50,
  "description": "Coffee",
  "expenseDate": "2026-09-01"
}

### Get it back by id → 200
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary with token → 200
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary without token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/summary

### Malformed token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token